  <p>If you're adding an accessory dwelling unit, a garage conversion, a junior ADU, or a detached new build in the backyard, one of the first things your designer or the building department will ask for is a set of as-built drawings of what's already there. Most homeowners don't expect this, and it's one of the most common reasons an ADU project stalls before it even reaches plan check.</p>

